# <Verb in imperative, capitalised> <what changed> — max ~72 chars
#
# Why this change exists. What it fixes or enables. What was verified and how.
# Wrap at 72. Reference issues as: Refs: #123 / Fixes: #123
#
# ── Required, enforced by .githooks ─────────────────────────────────────────
#   Signed-off-by: Your Name <you@robotis.com>     ← `git commit -s` adds this
#   GPG signature                                   ← commit.gpgsign = true
#
# The sign-off is a DCO attestation that you wrote the work or have the right
# to submit it. The GPG signature proves who committed it. Both are required;
# neither substitutes for the other.
#
# Subjects start with a capitalised verb, because CHANGELOG.rst is generated
# from them (ROBOTIS ROS Style Guide 4.6):
#   Added zero-copy path to the diff-drive controller
#   Fixed odometry drift when the encoder wraps
#   Removed the deprecated buzzer parameter
